{
  "id": "mcq-filter-blank-values",
  "unit": "filter-and-null",
  "mode": "choice",
  "tier": "medium",
  "title": "Which script produces this output?",
  "topics": [
    "filter",
    "isEmpty"
  ],
  "examObjective": "Predicting the result of core DataWeave functions",
  "prompt": "Given the payload below, **which script produces exactly this output?**\n\n```\n[ \"a\", \"b\", \"  \" ]\n```",
  "inputMime": "application/json",
  "outputMime": "application/json",
  "choice": {
    "kind": "which-script",
    "payload": "[\"a\",\"\",null,\"b\",\"  \"]",
    "target": "[ \"a\", \"b\", \"  \" ]",
    "answer": 3,
    "options": [
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter (isEmpty($))",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter ($ != null)",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter ($ != \"\")",
      "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter (not isEmpty($))"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [],
  "solution": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter (not isEmpty($))",
  "explanation": {
    "approach": "`isEmpty` is true for null and for the empty String, but a String of spaces is not empty. The two partial checks each let one of null and \"\" through.",
    "snippets": [
      {
        "label": "The answer",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter (not isEmpty($))",
        "payload": "[\"a\",\"\",null,\"b\",\"  \"]",
        "expect": {
          "output": "[ \"a\", \"b\", \"  \" ]"
        },
        "note": "The parentheses matter: `not` binds loosely."
      },
      {
        "label": "Only nulls removed",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter ($ != null)",
        "payload": "[\"a\",\"\",null,\"b\",\"  \"]",
        "expect": {
          "output": "[ \"a\", \"\", \"b\", \"  \" ]"
        },
        "note": "The empty String stays."
      },
      {
        "label": "Only empty Strings removed",
        "script": "%dw 2.0\noutput application/json\n---\npayload filter ($ != \"\")",
        "payload": "[\"a\",\"\",null,\"b\",\"  \"]",
        "expect": {
          "output": "[ \"a\", null, \"b\", \"  \" ]"
        },
        "note": "null is not equal to \"\", so it stays in."
      }
    ]
  }
}
